WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.350
An army of heroes and villains back from the
dead.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.600
An alien terrorist out for revenge.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.720
And a copycat robot powered cosmic by forces.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.610
Who are these villains the Avengers created?

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.500
The clearest example of the Avengers creating
a villain in the comics came when Dr. Hank

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:25.179
Pym combined his expertise in robotics, biology,
and chemistry, to build his greatest creation:

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:26.179
Ultron.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:31.300
Using his own brain patterns, Pym had no clue
that giving this robot a twisted version of

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.320
his own disturbed mind was asking for trouble.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.640
Barely mobile in his first form, Ultron came
to life immediately upon receiving human brain

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.489
patterns and immediately decided to rebel
against his "father."

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:49.019
Indeed, Ultron reacted to Pym with a murderous
Oedipus complex, wanting to kill and replace

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:50.019
him.

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:55.309
Ultron quickly evolved, later stealing the
impervious metal adamantium for his new bodies.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:01:00.880
No matter how many times he's seemingly been
destroyed for good, he's always had contingency

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.350
plans in place.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.890
His general hatred of humanity led him to
genocidal schemes like killing the entire

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.610
population of Slorenia.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.940
In the films, of course, it's Tony Stark who
builds Ultron with the help of Bruce Banner.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.600
The film Ultron gets his brain patterns with
a little help from Stark and the Mind Stone,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.400
and his actions ultimately lead to the destruction
of Sokovia.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.400
And we thought Tony was such a genius.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.170
"Don't compare me with Stark!

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.290
It's a thing with me.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.220
Stark is, he's a sickness!"

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:34.560
Kang was a 31st-century layabout named Nathaniel
Richards who was bored with the tranquility

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.520
of his era and was fascinated by watching
ancient recordings of heroes like the Fantastic

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.140
Four and the Avengers.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.860
When he stumbled upon a time machine, he used
it to travel to ancient Egypt, which he conquered

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.780
under the name Rama-Tut [ROM-uh TUT].

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.880
After then conquering the 40th century, Kang
decided to visit the 20th century to face

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.360
the legendary Avengers.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.970
There, he was defeated, and fighting the Avengers
became an obsession, leading to an infinite

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.910
number of alternate timelines — some in
which he beat the Avengers, some in which

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:07.460
he lost, and others where he fought against
himself.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.160
One of those possible versions of Kang was
an older iteration named Immortus who, having

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.120
grown weary of conflict, dedicated himself
to maintaining the timeline and protecting

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.810
it against the machinations of his younger
self.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:24.730
In this role, Immortus sometimes battled the
Avengers, and sometimes assisted them.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.410
How this will all play out in the MCU remains
to be seen.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:33.020
The Disney+ show "Loki" introduced a version
of Immortus called He Who Remains, and he

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:37.810
in turn introduced fans to the coming conflict
between an infinite number of Kangs battling

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.640
for the fate of the multiverse.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.910
With Kang set to appear in "Ant-Man and the
Wasp: Quantumania," it looks like the struggle

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:49.720
between Kang and the Avengers is likely to
take center stage in the MCU for years to

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:50.720
come.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.120
Early in the Avengers' career, Nazi scientist
Baron Heinrich Zemo realized that he couldn't

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.069
defeat his arch-enemy, Captain America, on
his own.

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:03.470
So he recruited the enemies of the other Avengers:
Thor's enemy Radioactive Man, Giant-Man's

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:08.130
enemy the Black Knight, and Iron Man's enemy
the Melter to beat them as the Masters of

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.130
Evil.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:12.420
That group failed, and later disbanded after
Baron Zemo's death.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.410
But it was just the first of many iterations
of the Master of Evil that have been formed

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:20.840
over the years, always by villains who hold
a grudge against the Avengers.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.530
Ultron, for instance, re-formed the team to
destroy his

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:28.890
"father" Hank Pym, while another Pym villain
- Egghead - later built a new version to disgrace

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.940
Pym and the Avengers.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.520
And the original Baron Zemo's son, Helmut
Zemo, also put together his own Master of

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.800
Evil to avenge his father's death.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.100
This time, he nearly succeeded, destroying
the Avengers' headquarters while capturing

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.820
and seriously injuring several members before
the reserves rallied to save the day.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.270
When the Avengers disappeared after fighting
a menace called Onslaught, Zemo later responded

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:56.830
by forming a new Masters of Evil that disguised
themselves as superheroes and dubbed them

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.459
the Thunderbolts.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:02.940
Given what a fan favorite the MCU version
of Helmut Zemo has become, it would be an

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:07.320
interesting twist to see him try to destroy
the superhero team from within after working

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.870
so hard to unsuccessfully destroy them from
without.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:17.650
Simon Williams was a scientific genius whose
company was a direct rival to Tony Stark.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.410
After Stark bankrupted him, he stole money
to stay afloat.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:25.669
He was arrested, but the Masters of Evil offered
him a chance at revenge.

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:30.819
He was given superpowers along with the name
Wonder Man in a scheme to infiltrate the Avengers

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:32.509
and destroy them from within.

00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:37.050
Instead, though, he sacrificed his own life
to save the team.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.759
Simon's brother Eric Williams then became
the supervillain known as the Grim Reaper

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:43.969
in order to get revenge on the Avengers for
Simon's death.

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:49.840
And he nearly succeeded: only the unexpected
intervention of the Black Panther saved the

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.569
Avengers from certain death.

00:04:51.569 --> 00:04:56.800
Even when Wonder Man returned from seeming
death and began a second career as an actor,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.300
the Grim Reaper regarded him as a fake version
of his brother.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:06.300
The Reaper also had a grudge against the Vision,
seeing him as someone who stole Simon's identity.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:12.069
The Reaper continued his crusade against the
Avengers even after he died and his subsequent

00:05:12.069 --> 00:05:15.460
resurrection, despite his “brothers” welcoming
him.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.490
So can we expect to see any of this in the
MCU?

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:23.669
Well, Simon Williams was briefly seen in a
deleted scene in Guardians of the Galaxy 2,

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:28.310
where, played by Nathan Fillion, he appeared
on a number of fake movie posters.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.580
And the character also appeared in concept
art for WandaVision.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:37.349
So fingers crossed we get to see Wonder Man
and Grim Reaper sooner rather than later!

00:05:37.349 --> 00:05:42.309
Remember the Grandmaster, who was played so
memorably in the films by Jeff Goldblum?

00:05:42.309 --> 00:05:43.930
"What's this?"

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:45.550
[gestures weirdly]

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.979
"Dial it down?"

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:53.630
Well, in the comics he's often gotten mixed
up in games that use the Avengers as pawns,

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:57.280
including one where the Grandmaster faced
off in a challenge against Kang.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.460
When Kang picked the Avengers to be his champions,
the Grandmaster created a new team to confront

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.360
them: the Squadron Sinister.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.569
Hyperion came to Earth as a baby from a doomed
Microverse planet.

00:06:08.569 --> 00:06:11.860
Nighthawk was a millionaire whose powers grew
stronger at night.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:15.830
Dr. Spectrum had a crystal that allowed him
to create energy constructs.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.500
And the Whizzer could run really fast.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.550
Sound familiar?

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:23.800
They should, because the team was intended
to be a joke version of the Justice League

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:29.030
of America and its members Superman, Batman,
Green Lantern, and Flash.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:33.680
The Squadron Sinister was defeated and broke
up, with Nighthawk becoming a superhero and

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.499
the others turning to solo crime.

00:06:35.499 --> 00:06:40.650
And to complicate things even more, an alternate
universe version of the team called the Squadron

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.960
Supreme where they are all good guys later
showed up.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.319
Don't expect to ever see either Squadron in
the MCU, though.

00:06:47.319 --> 00:06:51.969
We have a feeling the lawyers at AT&amp;T wouldn't
appreciate Marvel using the Justice League

00:06:51.969 --> 00:06:53.650
very much.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:58.680
Created by evil scientist group Advanced Idea
Mechanics, the Super Adaptoid's original function

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.830
was to destroy Captain America.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:05.949
With a sliver of the Cosmic Cube, aka the
Tesseract, this robot had the power to adapt

00:07:05.949 --> 00:07:08.889
to any opponent by copying their powers.

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:13.249
Which is where the Avengers come in, because
thanks to their might, a true monster was

00:07:13.249 --> 00:07:14.249
created.

00:07:14.249 --> 00:07:18.479
Super Adaptoid nearly killed Cap in their
first battle after absorbing the powers and

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:21.800
skills of the Wasp, Hawkeye, and Goliath.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.720
As if that wasn't bad enough, he ultimately
attempted to replace the entire population

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.300
of Earth with adaptoids.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.330
It would have worked if Captain America hadn't
tricked him by challenging him to copy the

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:36.569
most basic fact of being alive: death.

00:07:36.569 --> 00:07:40.169
The Super Adaptoid did, and promptly dropped
dead.

00:07:40.169 --> 00:07:43.219
If only Thanos had been that easy to trick!

00:07:43.219 --> 00:07:50.020
"You should have gone for the head!"

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:54.750
In the Operation: Galactic Storm storyline,
the Kree Supreme Intelligence deliberately

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.839
started a war knowing that his people would
lose.

00:07:57.839 --> 00:07:58.839
Why?

00:07:58.839 --> 00:08:03.869
He believed his race was at an evolutionary
dead end and wanted to find a way to kick-start

00:08:03.869 --> 00:08:08.020
their development, so he used the war as a
way to trick his people into detonating the

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.830
Nega-Bomb, which wiped out almost their entire
species.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:17.759
After failing to stop this scheme, a faction
of the Avengers led by Iron Man passed judgment

00:08:17.759 --> 00:08:21.669
on the Supreme Intelligence and executed him
for his war crimes.

00:08:21.669 --> 00:08:28.449
That, in turn, led some of the few surviving
Kree to vow vengeance on Earth and the Avengers.

00:08:28.449 --> 00:08:33.279
Led by Galen Kor, these Kree terrorists first
tried to blow up the Earth, then tried to

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:37.319
genetically mutate the population into Kree
to rebuild their own people.

00:08:37.319 --> 00:08:41.990
But Galen Kor and his group were ultimately
defeated, thanks in part to the reborn Supreme

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.089
Intelligence working against them.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:46.259
He had his own agenda.

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:50.949
Thanks to having a lot of enemies with connections
to either time travel or the afterlife, the

00:08:50.949 --> 00:08:55.019
Avengers have had to face multiple iterations
of the Legion of the Unliving.

00:08:55.019 --> 00:08:59.339
These villain teams consisted of dead friends
and foes that were either plucked from right

00:08:59.339 --> 00:09:03.319
before they died or yanked away from their
eternal rewards.

00:09:03.319 --> 00:09:08.649
Kang commanded the first version, which included
Wonder Man, Baron Heinrich Zemo, and the original

00:09:08.649 --> 00:09:09.649
Human Torch.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:13.839
Later, The Grandmaster cooked up a scheme
that involved sending the Avengers to Death's

00:09:13.839 --> 00:09:14.839
realm.

00:09:14.839 --> 00:09:20.270
He nearly won, but Hawkeye cheated in a game
of chance and Death was freed from the Grandmaster's

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.389
control, ending the contest.

00:09:22.389 --> 00:09:26.080
So could we ever see a Legion of the Unliving
in the MCU?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.889
It seems unlikely, but given that things like
the Marvel Zombies have begun appearing on

00:09:30.889 --> 00:09:33.209
"What If?," anything is possible!

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:37.300
The Grim Reaper took a cue from Baron Zemo
and formed his own team of villains with grudges

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.930
against the Avengers to help him out with
his own, which he called the Lethal Legion.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.519
After being defeated the first time around,
the Grim Reaper returned years later with

00:09:45.519 --> 00:09:47.040
an all new team.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:52.079
This time they battled the West Coast Avengers,
but while they had a power advantage, internal

00:09:52.079 --> 00:09:53.770
bickering broke the team up.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:57.959
Undeterred, the Grim Reaper put together a
third team which also failed.

00:09:57.959 --> 00:10:01.290
Hey, they are villains, their role is to lose
in these stories.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.959
There was also one other Lethal Legion of
note, also created specifically to oppose

00:10:05.959 --> 00:10:07.200
the Avengers.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.530
Count Nefaria, who had a long standing grudge
against the team, put together his own group.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:16.910
But they were unwitting dupes: Nefaria ended
up absorbing all of their powers to turn himself

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.079
into a literal superman.

00:10:19.079 --> 00:10:23.970
The moral of the story: never trust someone
named Nefaria!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:28.329
You may know Dane Whitman and Sersi from the
2021 Marvel film "Eternals."

00:10:28.329 --> 00:10:34.180
But you may not know that in the comics, their
romance nearly destroyed the entire multiverse.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:38.519
In the comics, Dane Whitman - also known as
the Black Knight - and Sersi were teammates.

00:10:38.519 --> 00:10:42.800
They got involved in a love triangle - she
was into him, he was into someone else - which

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.500
became problematic when Sersi's powers began
turning her unstable and dangerous.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.680
Dane was eventually psychically bonded with
her against his will to help control her powers.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.269
But that's not how it happened in every world.

00:10:55.269 --> 00:10:59.250
In another universe, Dane fell for Sersi but
she eventually ended up dumping him.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:06.529
So, in a supreme example of toxic masculinity,
the incel Dane killed Sersi and the Avengers

00:11:06.529 --> 00:11:11.620
and then began traveling to alternate universes,
hunting down Sersi in every reality.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:15.940
Changing his name to Proctor, he put together
a team of alternate universe Avengers to help

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:16.940
him.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.220
Called the Gatherers, most of these heroes
were tricked into thinking they were saving

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:25.079
the world from these "unstable" versions of
Sersi, unaware that it was Proctor himself

00:11:25.079 --> 00:11:28.810
who was using his powers to destabilize Sersi
in the first place.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:32.570
Ultimately, Proctor was killed by Sersi in
the main comic reality.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:38.339
Here's hoping that the MCU versions of these
characters have a much easier time of things!

00:11:38.339 --> 00:11:42.820
Of course, the movie Avengers have made just
as many messes as the comic Avengers.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:47.649
Besides Ultron, there's also Baron Helmut
Zemo, who vowed revenge on all superheroes

00:11:47.649 --> 00:11:51.339
after the Avengers failed to save his family
in the battle of Sokovia.

00:11:51.339 --> 00:11:52.720
And then there's the Battle of New York.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:58.329
Yes, the Avengers drove off the alien invasion,
but they left a giant mess both literally

00:11:58.329 --> 00:12:02.519
and figuratively - a mess that led to the
Vulture selling alien tech to the highest

00:12:02.519 --> 00:12:05.480
bidder after he was screwed out of his rightful
salvage contracts.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:10.339
Oh, and there's also Loki, who the Avengers
unleashed on the entire multiverse when their

00:12:10.339 --> 00:12:14.269
time-traveling trip to the battle's aftermath
went completely haywire.

00:12:14.269 --> 00:12:18.689
The Avengers: living proof that no good deed
goes unpunished.

00:12:18.689 --> 00:12:20.650
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.290
Plus, even more Looper videos about Marvel
are coming soon.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:26.810
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

